  "reproducibility_note": "Two builds of one commit are byte-identical only if the toolchain is deterministic. Next.js generates a random build id per build and cannot be told to pin it without a product configuration change, so the shipped bytes differ. This comparison therefore accounts for every difference by checking it: names that differ only by the build id, content that differs only by the build id, entries that record generated or builder-derived values, entries whose content differs only in the order it was written in, and the wheel's own index of its entries -- which is accounted for by the entries it indexes, once every one of those is named. Anything left over is the result, and nothing left over is the outcome a releasable artifact must produce.",
